  <main id="content">
    <section class="hero" id="top">
      <div class="container hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Membership-based worship network</p>
          <h1>Connecting and equipping worship leaders and musicians serving in local churches.</h1>
          <p>Sing His Praise exists to create a network of worship team leaders and members who can help strengthen the wider body of Christ. Its heart is to serve church plants, smaller churches, and other places of need where there may be real desire, but not always the resources, systems, or support needed to build a healthy and skillful worship team.</p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#join">Apply for membership</a>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#start-here">See the first 30 days</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-composition">
          <article class="hero-panel">
            <p class="eyebrow">Core structure</p>
            <h2>Website as home base. Community as daily rhythm.</h2>
            <p style="margin-top:1rem;color:var(--color-text-muted)">The public side should clearly communicate the vision, values, and invitation of Sing His Praise. The member side should guide people into teaching, community, practical training, and shared rhythms that help worship leaders and musicians grow in faithfulness and effectiveness in their local churches.</p>
            <div class="stats-grid">
              <div class="stat"><strong>6</strong><span>primary member lanes</span></div>
              <div class="stat"><strong>30</strong><span>days of guided onboarding</span></div>
              <div class="stat"><strong>1</strong><span>clear next step per screen</span></div>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <p class="eyebrow">Launch posture</p>
            <h3>Shared resources. Collective wisdom. Authentic fellowship.</h3>
            <p>Sing His Praise is designed to help people who may be carrying a lot with limited support. The goal is not to impress with scale, but to strengthen teams with wisdom, training, prayer, and practical connection.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="about">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">About Sing His Praise</p>
            <h2>Why Sing His Praise exists and who it is meant to serve.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Sing His Praise exists to strengthen the people who help shape worship in the local church, especially in communities where the need is great and the resources are limited. It was formed out of a desire to build something more thoughtful than a content vault and more grounded than a loose online chat space: a place where worship leaders, musicians, and ministry builders can grow in formation, craft, friendship, and service together.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillars" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))">
          <article class="card"><h3>Christ-Centered Worship</h3><p>We exist first and foremost to glorify Jesus Christ. Worship is not performance or preference, but a response to who God is and what He has done.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Kingdom Mindset</h3><p>We set our minds on things above and labor with a kingdom perspective, remembering that our service is ultimately for Christ and for the good of His Church.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Biblical Foundation</h3><p>Our practices, language, and theology of worship are rooted in Scripture and shaped by God’s Word, not by trends, personality, or preference.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Community</h3><p>We are called to encourage one another and build one another up. Sing His Praise is meant to be a place of authentic fellowship, shared wisdom, and mutual strengthening.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Growth</h3><p>We want to keep learning. As worship leaders and musicians, we pursue growth in skill, understanding, maturity, and the wisdom needed to serve well.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Next Generation</h3><p>We invest in and encourage upcoming worship leaders and musicians, helping them grow in confidence, calling, and capability for the years ahead.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Excellence</h3><p>We desire to offer our best to God. Excellence is not perfectionism, but faithful stewardship of the gifts, opportunities, and responsibilities He has given us.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Go</h3><p>We want our worship and our lives to serve the mission of God. As we grow, we also go—carrying the gospel, strengthening the Church, and serving where there is need.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="pathways">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Recommended site map</p>
            <h2>A structure that helps people understand the vision and take the next step.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>The site should make the mission easy to understand and the next steps easy to take. People should quickly see what Sing His Praise is, who it is for, and how it can help worship teams in church plants, smaller churches, and other places of need move toward greater health and quality.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="site-map">
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Vision and overview</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Home</li>
              <li>About / vision</li>
              <li>Membership overview</li>
              <li>Events & seminars</li>
              <li>Apply / contact</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Start Here</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Welcome page</li>
              <li>Start Here checklist</li>
              <li>Culture & expectations</li>
              <li>How the community layer works</li>
              <li>First-month milestones</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Resource library</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Worship topics</li>
              <li>Tutorials</li>
              <li>Leadership and team health</li>
              <li>Featured series</li>
              <li>Downloads and notes</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Community pathways</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Electric guitar</li>
              <li>Keys</li>
              <li>Vocals</li>
              <li>Bass</li>
              <li>MD and sound</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Leadership & development</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Point-person roles</li>
              <li>Christ-centered worship</li>
              <li>Care escalation</li>
              <li>Prayer rhythms</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Mission in action</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Prayer and encouragement board</li>
              <li>Gatherings</li>
              <li>Prayer requests and support</li>
              <li>Opportunities to serve and strengthen others</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="start-here">
      <div class="container two-col">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Start Here</p>
          <h2>The first month should feel grounded, clear, and encouraging.</h2>
          <p>Welcome to Sing His Praise. This is your first step into the life of the network. Rather than handing you everything at once, this page is meant to help you get oriented, understand the culture, and take a few meaningful first steps.</p>
          <div class="checklist">
            <div class="check"><strong>1</strong><div><h3>Welcome message</h3><p>Sing His Praise was built to serve people who are carrying real responsibility in worship ministry. Whether you lead a team, serve as a musician, help shape rehearsal culture, or support the technical side of worship, this space exists to strengthen you spiritually, practically, and relationally.</p></div></div>
            <div class="check"><strong>2</strong><div><h3>Find your lane</h3><p>Read the vision, complete your profile, and identify your primary role so Sing His Praise can guide you toward the most relevant spaces and resources.</p></div></div>
            <div class="check"><strong>3</strong><div><h3>Begin to participate</h3><p>Introduce yourself in the right space, engage one teaching resource, and take one meaningful step into the life of the community.</p></div></div>
            <div class="check"><strong>4</strong><div><h3>Build a sustainable rhythm</h3><p>By the end of the first month, the goal is simple: begin a healthy rhythm of learning, community, encouragement, and faithful service in your local church.</p></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="quote-block">
          <p>“One welcome email is not a strategy. The first month should move people from curiosity to confidence.”</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="member-home">
      <div class="wide">
        <div class="section-head" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-6)">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Member portal mockup</p>
